+"""Verified problem generator derived from arXiv:1706.08050.
+
+The paper's Theorem 4 reduces Connected Vertex Cover to Connected Odd Cycle
+Transversal by retaining every source edge and adding an even parallel path.
+For the p=3 case used here, that path has two edges, so every source edge is
+completed to a triangle.  This module inverse-generates a uniquely forced
+connected vertex cover and carries it through that exact construction.
+
+The graph is decorated with a polynomial over GF(998244353).  A generic exact
+route evaluates it at every vertex; the intended compact route recognizes a
+translated binomial and enumerates its root coset.  The graph witness is still
+checked directly, without trusting the decoration or the planted answer.
+"""
