+    "requiring the selected vertices to induce a connected graph. Section 2, "
+    "Theorem 4 is the construction used here: retain each source edge and add "
+    "a path of 2*floor(p/2) edges; at p=3 each source edge becomes a triangle, "
+    "and a connected vertex cover is carried unchanged to a connected odd-cycle "
+    "transversal. Theorem 4 proves NP-completeness for every fixed girth p>=3, "
+    "whereas Section 3, Theorems 10, 12, and 14 make the three connected "
+    "transversal problems polynomial-time on sP2-free graphs for every fixed s; "
+    "the generated cycle backbone has unbounded induced-matching number, so it "
+    "does not enter that easy regime. This is Track B because the supplied "
+    "finite-field annotation gives a polynomial-time recovery algorithm. The "
+    "certificate is nevertheless inverse-generated, not found by that algorithm: "
+    "the roots and the alternating source cover are sampled first, the source "
+    "graph is built around them, and Theorem 4 carries the same set forward. "
+    "Roots and decoys are both field elements; the source cycle balances their "
+    "basic incidence statistics. Degree outlier, greedy cover, random restart, "
+    "and an unshifted-binomial ansatz are measured in the adversary panel."
