index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4335db893a4c31988e6fc953b7f0c1915e30d4ce
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,169 @@
+# Verified generator for arXiv:1706.08050
+
+> **Status:** the generator and all local gates are complete, but this result is
+> not yet shippable.  The required four-vendor hardening run was attempted on
+> 2026-09-05 and OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded` on every
+> redraw.  G9(b) therefore remains unmeasured; no model error is counted as a
+> failure to solve.
+
+| profile field | value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B — no-tool compression** |
+| Native domain | combinatorics |
+| Object regime | finite field |
+| Computational core | polynomial identity |
+| Certificate | integer tuple (source-vertex labels) |
+| Intuition | change of variables |
+| Domain essentiality | licensed reduction |
+| Reduction | paper-licensed, Section 2, Theorem 4 at `p=3` |
+
+## Problem and provenance
+
+The family is based on Chiarelli, Hartinger, Johnson, Milanič, and Paulusma,
+[“Minimum Connected Transversals in Graphs”](https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.08050).
+The solver receives a labelled source graph `H`; every source edge is retained
+and completed to a triangle by a fresh vertex.  It must give exactly `n+1`
+source vertices, including a designated connector, whose deletion leaves the
+expanded graph bipartite and whose induced subgraph is connected.  Verification
+checks that the proposed set covers every source edge.  This simultaneously
+proves connectivity (through the connector) and leaves only a forest of
+subdivision leaves, so checking is linear in the displayed edge list.
+
+Generation samples the answer first.  Roots and decoys alternate on a spanning
+even cycle.  The two size-`n` covers of that cycle are its parity classes; one
+extra edge inside the root class rules out the decoy class.  Random cross-part
+edges add clutter without changing the unique size-`n` cover.  Theorem 4 then
+carries that connected cover unchanged to a connected odd-cycle transversal of
+the triangle expansion.  No generated instance is solved to obtain its answer.
+
+## Why Track B
+
+The paper proves Connected Odd Cycle Transversal NP-complete on every fixed
+girth class in Section 2, Theorem 4, but that is only worst-case evidence and is
+**not** claimed as distributional Track-A hardness here.  This distribution has
+an efficient algorithm: evaluate the displayed degree-`d` polynomial by Horner's
+rule on all `2d` labelled vertices.  At provisional shipping `d=64`, this costs
+16,640 counted modular multiplications/additions (`O(d^2)`) and about 0.0007 s in
+CPython.  The compact route notices that the polynomial is a translate of
+`y^d-1`, derives the translation from the next-to-leading coefficient, and
+walks the root-of-unity coset in 212 exact operations.  That is short enough for
+the no-tool cap but must be recognized and executed with nine-digit modular
+arithmetic.
+
+The easy regimes were explicitly avoided.  Section 3, Theorems 10, 12, and 14
+give polynomial algorithms for fixed `sP2`-free graphs via enumeration and the
+price of connectivity.  The generated cycle backbones have induced-matching
+number growing with `n`, so no fixed `s` contains the family.
+
+## Worked demo
+
+This is `render(make_instance(seed=7, n=4, clutter=1))` in full:
+
+```text
+Connected odd-cycle transversal in a triangle-expanded graph
+
+All graphs here are finite, simple, undirected graphs. A vertex set T is an
+odd-cycle transversal if deleting T leaves a bipartite graph (equivalently, a
+graph with no odd cycle). T is connected if the subgraph induced by T is
+connected.
+
+The source graph H has one connector vertex C and these 8 GF(998244353) vertices:
+423938499, 347712781, 161973069, 434296500, 51847156, 261129064,
+347712783, 698935572
+
+Its complete source-edge list is:
+(261129064,C) (161973069,261129064) (698935572,C)
+(261129064,423938499) (51847156,347712783) (261129064,347712783)
+(161973069,434296500) (347712783,698935572) (347712781,C)
+(261129064,698935572) (423938499,434296500) (423938499,C)
+(51847156,C) (51847156,347712781) (347712783,C) (161973069,C)
+(161973069,347712781) (434296500,C)
+
+Construct G by retaining every source edge {u,v} and, for each one, adding a
+fresh vertex q_e and edges {u,q_e},{q_e,v}; there are no other vertices or edges.
+
+F(x)=c[0]+...+c[4]x^4 over GF(998244353), low-to-high coefficients:
+105362238, 953896044, 855570738, 605637578, 1.
+The integer 3 is a primitive root modulo 998244353.
+
+Find exactly 5 source vertices forming a connected odd-cycle transversal of G,
+including C and exactly 4 field vertices. Do not output q_e. Encode C as
+998244353 and list distinct integers in strictly increasing order.
+
+Give the final answer inside <answer></answer> as comma-separated integers.
+```
+
+Answer:
+
+```text
+<answer>261129064, 347712781, 347712783, 434296500, 998244353</answer>
+```
+
+`verify` returns `(True, "ok")`.  Dropping the connector returns
+`(False, "wrong_length_expected_5")`.  A person can solve this smallest case by
+marking an endpoint of every displayed non-connector edge and checking the five
+candidate labels.
+
+## Presets and local gates
+
+| preset | `n` | clutter | answer atoms | status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 4 | 1 | 5 | hand-scale illustration |
+| easy | 32 | 64 | 33 | oracle run not completed |
+| medium | 64 | 128 | 65 | oracle run not completed |
+| hard | 64 | 512 | 65 | provisional shipping preset |
+
+| gate | measured result |
+|---|---|
+| G1 | 20/20 planted and JSON round-trip checks passed |
+| G2 | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | realistic prose/fence response round-tripped |
+| G4 | 0/200,000 structure-aware random guesses; space `C(128,64)` |
+| G5 | exactly one valid bounded witness; density about `4.18e-38`; reference 16,640 ops |
+| G6 | degree, greedy, 256-restart, and unshifted ansatz each 0/8; reference 8/8 |
+| G7 | doubled `n=128` instance built and verified; space grew from 124 to 251 bits |
+| G8 | 60/60 invariance and 60/60 carried-witness checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | 709 chars, 65 atoms, about 178 tokens, 212 intended operations |
+| G9(b) | **pending: OpenRouter quota blocked the required run** |
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 arms
+
+| arm/preset | seeds completed | solved | result |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| bare/easy | 0 | n/a | four redraws errored HTTP 403; harness aborted |
+| structural hint | 0 | n/a | not run after the same account-level error |
+| placebo hint | 0 | n/a | not run after the same account-level error |
+
+The hinted-minus-placebo diagnostic and the polarity-flipped G9(b) gate cannot
+be inferred from API errors.  Once the OpenRouter key is replenished, rerun the
+commands below and replace this table from the generated transcripts.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+import gen_1706_08050 as g
+
+inst = g.make_instance(seed=7, **g.DIFFICULTY["demo"])
+print(g.render(inst))
+candidate = g.parse_answer("<answer>" + ", ".join(map(str, inst["answer"])) + "</answer>")
+assert g.verify(inst, candidate) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+After the oracle quota is restored, run `python3 ../../scripts/harden.py
+gen_1706_08050.py`, run the structural and placebo copies in separate scratch
+directories, update `G9_RESULTS`, rerun `selftest`, and then emit from the repo
+root with `bash scripts/emit.sh 1706.08050`.
+
+## Caveats
+
+The polynomial annotation intentionally makes this a Track-B family: a CAS or
+128 Horner evaluations solves it quickly.  The guess probability is uniform
+over size-`n` field subsets after enforcing connector, shape, ordering, and
+distinctness; it is not a model of guesses biased by the polynomial.  The panel
+does not include a full ILP/SAT solver or a specialized minimum-vertex-cover
+implementation, although the polynomial reference algorithm is strictly enough
+to solve every generated instance.  Canonicalization is exact for input reorder
+and the family's global field-translation symmetry; it is not a complete
+canonical labeller for arbitrary uncoloured graph isomorphism because the field
+tags are semantic vertex data.  Most importantly, no oracle-hardness claim is
+made until the missing bare, hinted, and placebo runs complete successfully.
