codex
Step 0 supports a native graph family, but the prior triage’s “hit all forbidden substructures” description is too vague. The paper’s exact usable object is a connected odd-cycle transversal: a vertex set whose deletion leaves a bipartite graph and whose induced subgraph is connected. Theorem 2 supplies a particularly useful line-graph construction from an even cycle factor, while Section 3 warns that fixed-\(s\), \(sP_2\)-free instances are polynomial-time and should be avoided for Track A. I’m now testing whether the theorem’s construction can yield a genuinely hard planted distribution without leaking the factor.
