| medium | 16 | 225 | 849 | 145 | not reached |
| hard | 24 | 337 | 1,273 | 217 | provisional shipping preset |

| gate | measured result |
|---|---|
| G1 | 20/20 planted witnesses verified and JSON-round-tripped |
| G2 | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
| G3 | realistic prose/fence response round-tripped; garbage rejected |
| G4 | 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses; effective space `2^24`; exact density `2^-24` |
| G5 | one canonical completion; demo brute force = 1; Gaussian baseline 3,466 XORs on the fixed reporting seed |
| G6 | four attacks 0/8; Gaussian, DPLL, and compact references each 8/8 |
| G7 | `n=48` builds and verifies; search bits grow 24 to 48 (output then exceeds the shipping cap) |
| G8 | 60/60 invariance and carried-witness checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
| G9(c) | 1,002 chars, 251 estimated tokens, 217 atoms, 119 exact operations |
| G9(b) | **pending because the oracle account returned HTTP 403** |

The full unconstrained output grammar contains `3^24` valid clause-completion
variants, but guessing those independently is not an honest solver prior. G4
therefore samples one random variable assignment and completes its clauses
deterministically; its success probability is the unique-assignment density
`1/2^24 = 5.960464477539063e-08`.

