codex
Implemented and locally verified the Track B generator based on the paper’s Theorem 4 triangle expansion.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1706.08050/gen_1706_08050.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1706.08050/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1706.08050/README.md)
- [Blocking report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1706.08050/BLOCKED.md)
- [Partial oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1706.08050/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1706.08050/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1706.08050/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- G1–G9(c) pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Exact valid-answer density: \(2.65\times10^{-42}\).
- Four heuristic attacks: 0/8 each.
- Gaussian reference: 2,678 median XORs, 8/8 solved.
- Compact route: 119 XORs.
- Shipping answer: 217 atoms, 1,002 characters.
- Direct expanded-graph connectivity and bipartiteness check: 20/20.
- An alternative non-planted witness was also accepted.

The result is blocked, not rejected or shipped. The oracle pool solved all three `easy` calls and two `medium` calls, after which OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 total-quota errors. No `hard` call or scored G9 arm completed, so there is no honest shipping hardness verdict. The invalid artifact created when `submit.sh` mistakenly accepted the incomplete transcript was moved to `/tmp/1706.08050.invalid_emit.jsonl`, and the claim was restored to `in_progress`.

Paper source: [arXiv:1706.08050](https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.08050).
